---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import PageHeader from '../components/PageHeader.astro';
import { href } from '../lib/url';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About"
  description="Why Floor Life exists: a curious, welcoming field guide to movement, comfortable spaces, and life a little closer to the ground."
>
  <PageHeader
    eyebrow="The story & the method"
    title="About Floor Life"
    lede="A small internet corner for people wondering what happens when life comes down a level. Some movement, some home design, and a healthy respect for the words “we don’t know.”"
  />

  <div class="prose prose-floor mx-auto mt-12 max-w-2xl px-5 pb-8 sm:px-8">
    <p>Floor Life is an independent exploration by Christopher Smothers. It brings together practical position guides, room ideas, and an honest reading of research. The aim is to make an ordinary day feel a little more varied and a little less automatic.</p>
    <p>We borrow no claim to have invented living low. Floor-based traditions belong to many cultures, each with its own history and meaning. This site offers an invitation to explore what suits your home and body.</p>
    <p>If you like the mood, meet our sibling guide, <a href="https://deadbutt.fyi/">deadbutt.fyi</a>. Same affection for small useful changes; a slightly cheekier anatomical department.</p>

    <h2>What we believe</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Honesty is the whole brand.</strong> Every strong claim gets its
        caveat. When the evidence is thin, we say so. Being trusted is worth more
        than sounding impressive.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Retrofit, don't evangelise.</strong> You don't have to go
        furniture-free. One inviting corner beats a vow you'll break by Thursday.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Variety over dogma.</strong> There is no single correct posture.
        The goal is to own many and move between them — without making any one of them compulsory.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Beauty is functional.</strong> A floor you want to be on is a
        floor you'll use. A little charm can make trying something feel less like homework.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Who it's for</h2>
    <p>
      The floor-curious taking their first cushion down, and the seasoned
      floor-sitter going deeper. Start with <a href={href('/why')}>the evidence</a>,
      or just <a href={href('/start')}>get down on the floor</a> and see how it
      feels.
    </p>

    <p class="text-sm text-inkmuted">
      Not medical advice — see the <a href={href('/disclosure')}>disclosure</a>.
    </p>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
